    "media:imagetext": "HE SKAYAVENING POSI\nMarch 6, 1954\nFLondon\nE Youll never fly in such\n*Therp'es charmingness shout the way Pan\nAmerican waits on children.\" TV star Maria Riva\nreports. \"I know, you see, because I flew with\nmy two from New York to Rome on The President\nSpecial. Pan American gives you such a feeling of\ncomfort and security when you're flying with\nchildren. Von cet yury. ves. but on Pan\nAmerican you get experience, too... Flying an\nocean. that's unbortant?\nsays talented MARIA RIVA, stage and TV\nstar, who has crossed the Atlantic 29 times\nWHETHER YOU CHOOSE the extr-fare President Special, or\nPan American's famous tourist service-The Rainbow—\nor any Pan American service throughout the world, you get\nthese exclusive advantases: the unmatched record of Pan\nAmerican's Flight Crews (1200 Pan American pilots have flown\nover a million miles... 100 have flown over three million miles)\n... and the largest, most modern fleet of airliners in overseas\nservice. For reservations, call your Travel Agent or Pan American.\nTHE SATURDAY EVENING POST\nLower deck lounge. \"It's fun to be able to go down-\nbig, double-decked \"Strato' Clippers\" are roomy, too\nstairs on an airplane!\" says Maria Riva. \"Upstairs those | with a big, wide aisle and comfortable, tip-back seats.\"\nluxury as 'THE PRESIDENT SPECIAL\"\nOvernight... Non-Stop to PARIS and to LONDON...\nNothing finer flies the Atlantic than The President Special!\nThere's a sumptuous buffet table... a seven-course dinner\nby Maxim's of Paris-preceded by cocktails, graced with\nvintage champagne, followed by a fine liqueur. Bed-length\nSleeperette* service; or berths, available at extra cost. Orchids\nand Carven's perfume. Limited passenger list. Small surcharge.\nMom pople Sly to Bumpe by PAL AMERICAN\nWorld's Most Experienced Airline",
